```
# ============================================================================
# Detection: UAC Bypass via Auto-Elevate Binary Abuse
# Detection ID: DE-PR-002
# MITRE ATT&CK: T1548.002 - Abuse Elevation Control Mechanism: Bypass User Account Control
# Data Source: Sysmon EventCode=1
# Severity: High
# ============================================================================

index=endpoint sourcetype="XmlWinEventLog:Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational" EventCode=1
ParentImage IN ("*\\fodhelper.exe","*\\computerdefaults.exe","*\\sdclt.exe","*\\eventvwr.exe")
Image NOT IN ("*\\dllhost.exe","*\\conhost.exe")
| stats count min(_time) as first_seen values(CommandLine) as cmd values(Image) as child by ComputerName, User, ParentImage
| eval first_seen=strftime(first_seen,"%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S")
```

## Detection Logic
Auto-elevating Windows binaries like fodhelper.exe and computerdefaults.exe are frequently abused via registry hijacking (HKCU\\Software\\Classes\\...) to spawn an elevated child process without a UAC prompt. A child process outside the expected Explorer/COM handler set indicates abuse.

## False Positive Considerations
Rare — these binaries have very limited legitimate child-process behavior. Validate any hits manually rather than broad exclusion.

## Tuning Notes
Pair with a Sysmon 13 registry search for writes to the associated HKCU Classes keys to catch the setup stage before execution.
